---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";

const lastUpdated = new Date().toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
  year: "numeric",
  month: "long",
});
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Code Like It's 198x - How we protect your privacy and handle data in compliance with UK GDPR."
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        title="Privacy Policy"
        subtitle={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated}`}
        variant="centered"
      />

      <div class="legal-content">
        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">1. Introduction</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Code Like It's 198x ("we", "our", or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy and
            complying with the UK General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data
            Protection Act 2018. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle information when you use
            our website.
          </p>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We are a privacy-focused educational platform. We believe in minimal data collection and
            maximum transparency. This website is designed to function without requiring personal
            information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">2. Data Controller</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            For the purposes of UK data protection law, the data controller for this website is:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>Website: Code Like It's 198x</li>
            <li>
              Contact: Via GitHub at <a
                href="https://github.com/code198x"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="legal-section__link">github.com/code198x</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>Location: United Kingdom</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">3. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We operate on a principle of minimal data collection. Here's what we do and don't
            collect:
          </p>

          <p class="legal-section__text">
            <strong>What We DON'T Collect:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>No user accounts or registration data</li>
            <li>No names, email addresses, or contact information</li>
            <li>No tracking cookies or advertising cookies</li>
            <li>No third-party analytics (Google Analytics, etc.)</li>
            <li>No social media tracking pixels</li>
            <li>No behavioural tracking or profiling</li>
            <li>No payment or financial information</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="legal-section__text">
            <strong>What We MAY Collect:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>
              <strong>Server logs:</strong> Basic access logs (IP address, timestamp, pages visited)
              for security and debugging purposes only
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Local storage:</strong> Theme preferences stored only in your browser, never transmitted
              to servers
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Essential cookies:</strong> If implemented, only for essential website functionality
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Under UK GDPR, we must have a lawful basis for processing any personal data. Our lawful
            bases are:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>
              <strong>Legitimate interests (Article 6(1)(f)):</strong> For maintaining website security
              and preventing abuse through minimal server logging
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Legal obligations (Article 6(1)(c)):</strong> Where we need to comply with legal
              requirements
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We do not rely on consent as we do not collect personal data for marketing or
            non-essential purposes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">5. How We Use Information</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Any minimal data we collect through server logs is used solely for:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>Ensuring website security and preventing abuse</li>
            <li>Debugging technical issues and errors</li>
            <li>Complying with legal obligations</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We never use data for marketing, advertising, profiling, or selling to third parties.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">6. Data Retention</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">We follow these retention periods:</p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> Automatically deleted after 30 days</li>
            <li><strong>Local storage:</strong> Remains in your browser until you clear it</li>
            <li><strong>GitHub contributions:</strong> Subject to GitHub's retention policies</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">7. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            When you interact with our project through third-party services, you are subject to
            their privacy policies:
          </p>

          <p class="legal-section__text">
            <strong>GitHub</strong><br />
          </p>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            If you contribute code, open issues, or participate in discussions on GitHub, you are
            subject to <a
              href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="legal-section__link">GitHub's Privacy Policy</a
            >. We only see information that GitHub makes publicly available.
          </p>

          <p class="legal-section__text">
            <strong>Discord</strong><br />
          </p>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            If you join our community Discord server, you are subject to
            <a
              href="https://discord.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="legal-section__link">Discord's Privacy Policy</a
            >. We do not have access to your Discord account information beyond what you share
            publicly.
          </p>

          <p class="legal-section__text">
            <strong>Web Hosting</strong><br />
          </p>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Our website hosting provider may collect basic access logs in accordance with their
            privacy policy. We have ensured our hosting provider is GDPR-compliant.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">8. Your Rights Under UK GDPR</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Under UK data protection law, you have the following rights:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li><strong>Right to be informed:</strong> This privacy policy fulfils this right</li>
            <li><strong>Right of access:</strong> Request what personal data we hold about you</li>
            <li><strong>Right to rectification:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
            <li><strong>Right to erasure:</strong> Request deletion of your personal data</li>
            <li><strong>Right to restrict processing:</strong> Request limitation of processing</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Right to data portability:</strong> Receive your data in a portable format
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Right to object:</strong> Object to processing based on legitimate interests
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Rights related to automated decision making:</strong> We do not use automated decision
              making
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            To exercise any of these rights, please contact us through GitHub. Note that since we
            collect minimal data, we may not hold any personal data about you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">9. International Transfers</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Your information may be transferred to and processed in countries outside the UK, such
            as when using GitHub (US-based) or other international services. Where this happens, we
            ensure appropriate safeguards are in place, such as:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>Services that are covered by adequacy decisions</li>
            <li>Services using Standard Contractual Clauses approved by the UK ICO</li>
            <li>Other appropriate safeguards under UK GDPR</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">10. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Our website is educational and suitable for all ages. We do not knowingly collect
            personal data from children under 13. Since we don't require registration or collect
            personal information, children can safely use our educational resources.
          </p>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            Parents and teachers are encouraged to supervise children's use of the internet,
            including this website.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">11. Data Security</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect any data we
            process:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>HTTPS encryption for all website traffic</li>
            <li>Regular security updates and patches</li>
            <li>Minimal data collection philosophy</li>
            <li>Open source code for transparency</li>
            <li>No storage of sensitive personal data</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">12. Cookies Policy</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We believe in a cookie-free experience wherever possible:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>
              <strong>No tracking cookies:</strong> We don't use cookies for tracking or analytics
            </li>
            <li><strong>No advertising cookies:</strong> We don't serve ads or use ad networks</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Essential functionality only:</strong> If we implement cookies, they will be strictly
              necessary for website operation
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Local storage:</strong> Theme preferences are stored locally in your browser, not
              as cookies
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">13. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices
            or legal requirements. We will notify you of any material changes by:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>Updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this policy</li>
            <li>Posting a notice on our website homepage for significant changes</li>
            <li>Including a note in our GitHub repository for contributors</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">14. Complaints</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            If you have concerns about how we handle your data, you have the right to lodge a
            complaint with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO):
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>
              Website: <a
                href="https://ico.org.uk"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="legal-section__link">ico.org.uk</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>Phone: 0303 123 1113</li>
            <li>Live chat: Available on the ICO website</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We would appreciate the opportunity to address your concerns before you approach the
            ICO, so please contact us first.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2 class="legal-section__title">15. Contact Information</h2>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            For any questions about this Privacy Policy or to exercise your rights:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-section__list">
            <li>
              Open an issue on our <a
                href="https://github.com/code198x"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="legal-section__link">GitHub repository</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              Join our <a href="/community" class="legal-section__link">community discussion</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="legal-section__text">
            We aim to respond to all data protection enquiries within 30 days in accordance with UK
            GDPR.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-footer">
        <p class="legal-footer__text">
          This privacy policy was written to be clear, transparent, and easy to understand. We
          believe privacy is a fundamental right and design our services accordingly.
        </p>
        <nav class="legal-footer__nav">
          <a href="/terms" class="legal-footer__link">Terms of Service</a>
          <span class="legal-footer__separator">•</span>
          <a href="/sitemap" class="legal-footer__link">Sitemap</a>
          <span class="legal-footer__separator">•</span>
          <a href="/" class="legal-footer__link">Home</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ============================================
     Legal Page Styles (BEM) - Shared with Terms
     ============================================ */

  .legal-page {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal-content {
    margin: var(--space-2xl) 0;
  }

  /* Section Styles */
  .legal-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
    position: relative;
  }

  .legal-section:not(:last-of-type)::after {
    content: "";
    display: block;
    width: 100px;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-border-light) 0%, transparent 100%);
    margin: var(--space-2xl) auto;
  }

  .legal-section__title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-primary-lighter);
    position: relative;
  }

  .legal-section__title::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    bottom: -2px;
    left: 0;
    width: 40px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }

  .legal-section__text {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal-section__text:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* List Styles */
  .legal-section__list {
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal-section__list li {
    position: relative;
    padding: var(--space-md);
    padding-left: var(--space-2xl);
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-base);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    transition: var(--transition-base);
  }

  .legal-section__list li:hover {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-color: var(--color-primary-lighter);
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  .legal-section__list li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
  }

  .legal-section__list li strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    display: inline-block;
    margin-right: var(--space-xs);
  }

  /* Link Styles */
  .legal-section__link {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: var(--transition-base);
  }

  .legal-section__link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .legal-section__link[target="_blank"]::after {
    content: " ↗";
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* Footer Styles */
  .legal-footer {
    margin-top: var(--space-3xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-border);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .legal-footer__text {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .legal-footer__nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .legal-footer__link {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    transition: var(--transition-base);
  }

  .legal-footer__link:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .legal-footer__separator {
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
  }

  /* Dark Mode */
  .dark-mode .legal-section__title {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-border);
  }

  .dark-mode .legal-section__title::after {
    background: var(--color-primary-light);
  }

  .dark-mode .legal-section__list li {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-color: var(--color-border);
  }

  .dark-mode .legal-section__list li:hover {
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border-color: var(--color-primary-lighter);
  }

  .dark-mode .legal-section__list li::before {
    color: var(--color-primary-light);
  }

  .dark-mode .legal-footer {
    border-top-color: var(--color-border);
  }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .container {
      padding: 0 var(--space-md);
    }

    .legal-section__title {
      font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    }

    .legal-section__list {
      margin-left: 0;
    }

    .legal-section__list li {
      padding-left: var(--space-xl);
    }

    .legal-footer__nav {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-sm);
    }

    .legal-footer__separator {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
